[38;2;124;124;124mWait, $(t^2-t)^2 = t^2(t+1)^2$. Yes. So the identity checks out.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow let me verify invariance. Let $u = \frac{(t^2+t+1)^3}{t^2(t+1)^2}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mUnder $t \mapsto t+1$: $t^2+t+1 \mapsto (t+1)^2+(t+1)+1 = t^2+2t+1+t+1+1 = [0m
