[38;2;124;124;124m\mapsto t+1$. [0m

[38;2;124;124;124mUnder $t \mapsto 1/t$: $t^2+t+1 \mapsto 1/t^2 + 1/t + 1 = (1+t+t^2)/t^2 = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(t^2+t+1)/t^2$. And $t^2(t+1)^2 \mapsto (1/t^2)((1/t)+1)^2 = (1/t^2)((1+t)/t)^2 [0m[38;2;124;124;124m= (1+t)^2/t^4 = (t+1)^2/t^4$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo $u \mapsto \frac{((t^2+t+1)/t^2)^3}{(t+1)^2/t^4} = \frac{(t^2+t+1)^3/t^6}[0m
